Scenario ID: S08
Scenario title: Meeting Room Reservation
Initial workflow description:
A meeting room is reserved for a team meeting. The organizer checks availability and shares the room information with participants.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer use to check room availability and submit the reservation request?",
      "answer": "The organizer uses a dedicated room booking platform alongside a scheduling tool to look up open slots and submit the booking. These two tools work together so the organizer can confirm whether a space is free before locking it in."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Is any approval or confirmation required from a facilities team or administrator before the reservation is considered confirmed?",
      "answer": "No explicit approval step from a facilities manager or administrator is described. Once the organizer selects and reserves the room, the booking is treated as confirmed without a separate sign-off gate."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What happens when the requested room or time slot is already booked — does the organizer manually search for alternatives, or does the system suggest them?",
      "answer": "When no suitable space is free, the organizer goes back to searching for another option. The workflow does not specify that the platform automatically proposes alternatives; the fallback handling is listed as an exception but the resolution method is not detailed."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How is the confirmed room information communicated to participants, and is that notification step currently manual or automated?",
      "answer": "After securing the room, the organizer sends out a meeting invite and separately notifies attendees of the venue details using a messaging or collaboration tool. Both steps are attributed to the organizer, suggesting they are manually initiated rather than automatically triggered."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How are cancellations or changes to an existing reservation initiated and communicated to both the system and the participants?",
      "answer": "The workflow flags reservation conflicts and shifts in attendee numbers as known exceptions, but it does not spell out a defined cancellation or amendment procedure. How those changes get communicated back to the booking platform or to attendees is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Are there any required actions after the meeting concludes, such as formally releasing the room or logging whether the room was actually used?",
      "answer": "No post-meeting steps are described in the workflow. There is no mention of formally freeing the space, recording actual usage, or any other wrap-up obligation once the meeting ends."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
